# Shell scripts run inside a Linux container/shell and need a real LF
# shebang line to exec at all -- a CRLF-mangled `#!/bin/sh` fails with
# "no such file or directory", not a parse error, which is what broke the
# Cloud Run deploy after scripts/entrypoint.sh silently picked up CRLF on a
# Windows checkout (core.autocrlf converts on checkout; `gcloud builds
# submit` uploads the local working tree directly, not a git clone, so that
# conversion ships straight into the image). Force LF regardless of the
# checkout platform so this can't recur.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
